    "result_text": "The build succeeded and the acceptance test passes. There's a single test class (`AcceptanceTest`), and its assertion on `$.bulkSignupWarning == false` passing confirms the field is generated in the DTO, mapped from the entity, and returned correctly.\n\n## Summary\n\nI implemented the `bulkSignupWarning` flag as a **stored, captured-at-creation** field, following the exact pattern the codebase already uses for other derived-at-creation attributes like `namesakeCount` and `membershipNumber` (persisted once, then returned unchanged on every subsequent read).\n\n**Changes:**\n\n1. **`OwnerRestControllerV1.addOwner`** \u2014 the logic lives here alongside the existing daily-count rule. I hoisted the single `countOwnersRegisteredOn(registrationDate)` call into a local, reused it for both the hard daily-limit check (`>= 100`) and the new warning, and set `owner.setBulkSignupWarning(ownersRegisteredToday > 80)`. Added a `BULK_SIGNUP_WARNING_THRESHOLD = 80` constant next to `MAX_OWNERS_PER_DAY`, so both day-based rules sit together. This reuses the existing count rather than adding a second query.\n\n2. **`Owner` entity** \u2014 added a `bulkSignupWarning` `Boolean` field with `@Column(name = \"bulk_signup_warning\")`, getter, and setter.\n\n3. **`openapi.yml`** \u2014 added a read-only `bulkSignupWarning` boolean to the `Owner` schema so the generated `OwnerDto` carries it and MapStruct maps it automatically (no mapper changes needed).\n\n4. **Schema SQL** (hsqldb, h2, postgres, mysql) \u2014 added the `bulk_signup_warning` column.\n\n**Semantics:** \"more than 80 owners already created today\" \u2192 `ownersRegisteredToday > 80` (i.e. the 82nd+ owner of the day is flagged). The value is always set to `true`/`false` (never null) at creation, satisfying the \"otherwise false\" requirement, and is returned on both the create and `GET /api/owners/{id}` responses.",
